<title>ARGENTINA: RUGBY UNION-BUENOS AIRES BEAT ENGLAND 23-21.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BUENOS AIRES BEAT ENGLAND 23-21.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buenos Aires beat England 23-21 (halftime 11-11) at the Buenos Aires Cricket and Rugby Ground on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Tries: Ben Clark, Phil de Glanville, Jim Mallinder. Penalties: Alex King (2).</p>
<p>Buenos Aires - Try: Tomas Solari. Penalties: Jose Cilley (5). Drop goal: Cilley.</p>
</text>
